<title>USA: CUNO Inc Q1 Jan 31 net rises.</title>
<headline>CUNO Inc Q1 Jan 31 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MERIDEN, Conn. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>STATEMENTS OF CONSOLIDATED INCOME</p>
<p>						     THREE MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>							    January 31,</p>
<p>(in thousands, except per share</p>
<p>   and common share data)			1997	   1996</p>
<p> Net sales					$ 44,839     $ 41,004</p>
<p> Operating income				  3,927	  2,636</p>
<p> Net income					  2,065	  1,851</p>
<p> Earnings per share of common stock	   0.15	   0.14</p>
<p>Pro forma earnings per share of</p>
<p> common stock					 0.15	   0.11</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares outstanding</p>
<p>						  13,565,922   13,565,922</p>
<p>NOTE: Prior year pro forma earnings per share figure reflects a pro forma adjustment in interest expense and related tax to account for the allocation of $30 million in parent company debt to CUNO, assuming the Sept 10, 1996, distribution had taken place on Nov 1, 1995.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
